/*******************************************************************************
 * CHIP:  PHY8806X
 * REGISTER:  FCM_FCME_CONFIG
 * BLOCKS:   MAPPER
 * DESC:     This register allows general configuation of the FCM_Mapper in the egress direction.
 * SIZE:     32
 * FIELDS:
 *     CRC_REGEN_MODE   This mode allows the FC frame within the FCoE packet to be modified by an external switch with FCM_Mapper handling the CRC recomputation.1'b1 - No_CRC_Check_Mode;       FC-CRC is not checked by mapper, value is always considered good.       Good FC CRC is regenerated even in the absence of header modifications as long as Ethernet-FCS is good and no RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.        Bad FC-CRC is regenerated when the FC frame header is modified by the mapper and Ethernet-FCS is bad or FCoE packet has RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.       Incoming FC-CRC is preserved when the FC frame header is not modified by the mapper and Ethernet-FCS is bad or FCoE packet has RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.1'b0 - Normal_Mode;       Register bit "fcm_fcme_config_dbg_ignore_crc", OUI-CRC-Regen mode, FC-Frame-header-modification, Ethernet-FCS, FC-CRC, RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC are checked before regenerating CRC.       if the OUI-CRC-Regen mode is on, functionality is same as Register bit "fcm_fcme_config_crc_regen_mode" is set to 1.       if the OUI-CRC-Regen mode is off and Register bit "fcm_fcme_config_dbg_ignore_crc" is set to 0, following are the functionality,       Good FC-CRC is regenerated when the FC frame header is modified by the mapper and FC-CRC is good and Ethernet-FCS is good and no RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.       Bad FC-CRC is regenerated when the FC frame header is modified by the mapper and FC-CRC is bad or Ethernet-FCS is bad or RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.       Incoming FC-CRC is preserved when the FC frame header is not modified by the mapper.if the both register bits "fcm_fcme_config_crc_regen_mode" and "fcm_fcme_config_dbg_ignore_crc" are set to 1, the functionality depend on "fcm_fcme_config_dbg_ignore_crc" bit.
 *     DBG_IGNORE_CRC   Ignore CRC (both Ethernet-FCS and FC-CRC) debug mode.1'b1 - No_FCS_CRC_Check_Mode;       Both Ethernet-FCS and FC-CRC are not checked by the mapper, both are always considered good.       Good FC-CRC is regenerated even in the absence of header modifications as long as no RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.       Bad FC-CRC is regenerated when the FC frame header is modified by the mapper and FCoE packet has RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.       Incoming FC-CRC is preserved when the FC frame header is not modified by the mapper and FCoE packet has RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.1'b0 - Normal_Mode;       Register bit "fcm_fcme_config_crc_regen_mode", OUI-CRC-Regen mode, FC-Frame-header-modification, Ethernet-FCS, FC-CRC, RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC are checked before regenerating CRC.       if the OUI-CRC-Regen mode is on, functionality is same as Register bit "fcm_fcme_config_crc_regen_mode" is set to 1.       if the OUI-CRC-Regen mode is off and Register bit "fcm_fcme_config_crc_regen_mode" is set to 0, following are the functionality,       Good FC-CRC is regenerated when the FC frame header is modified by the mapper and FC-CRC is good and Ethernet-FCS is good and no RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.       Bad FC-CRC is regenerated when the FC frame header is modified by the mapper and FC-CRC is bad or Ethernet-FCS is bad or RX/ECC/Truncated-Packet error indication from CLMAC.       Incoming FC-CRC is preserved when the FC frame header is not modified by the mapper.if the both register bits "fcm_fcme_config_crc_regen_mode" and "fcm_fcme_config_dbg_ignore_crc" are set to 1, the functionality depend on "fcm_fcme_config_dbg_ignore_crc" bit.
 *     USE_IP_COS_MAP   Use IPV4-DSCP/IPV6-TC to CoS Map Value.                    This field is used by both the system side egress mapper (SSEM) and the line side ingress mapper (LSIM) only in bypass mode.
 *     DEFAULT_COS      Default CoS Value.                    This field is used by both the system side egress mapper (SSEM) and the line side ingress mapper (LSIM).
 *     FCOE_VERSION_CHECK_DISABLE Disable the FCoE Header Version field check:                       1 = fcoe version check disabled.                       0 = fcoe version check enabled.
 *     PASS_PAUSE_FRAME Pass the PAUSE FRAME in bypass mode:  1'b1 : PAUSE frames are passed to output. 1'b0 : PAUSE frames are dropped in SSEM/LSIM.                         This field is used by both the system side egress mapper (SSEM) and the line side ingress mapper (LSIM) only in bypass mode.                         This field is don't care in FC Mode. PAUSE frames are always dropped by SSEM in FC mode.
 *     PASS_PFC_FRAME   Pass the PFC FRAME in bypass mode:  1'b1 : PFC frames are passed to output. 1'b0 : PFC frames are dropped in SSEM/LSIM.                         This field is used by both the system side egress mapper (SSEM) and the line side ingress mapper (LSIM) only in bypass mode.                         This field is don't care in FC Mode. PFC frames are always dropped by SSEM in FC mode.
 *     PASS_CONTROL_FRAME Pass the CONTROL FRAME in bypass mode:  1'b1 : CONTROL frames are passed to output. 1'b0 : CONTROL frames are dropped in SSEM/LSIM.                         This field is used by both the system side egress mapper (SSEM) and the line side ingress mapper (LSIM) only in bypass mode.                         This field is don't care in FC Mode. CONTROL frames are always dropped by SSEM in FC mode.
 *
 ******************************************************************************/
