/*******************************************************************************
 * CHIP:  PHY8806X
 * REGISTER:  FCPORT_TOP_CTRL_CONFIG
 * BLOCKS:   LINE_FCPORT SYS_FCPORT
 * DESC:     Main Control bits for FCPORT, rw
 * SIZE:     32
 * FIELDS:
 *     UCMEM_ACCESS_CONTROL PORT to TSC micro-controller Memory (extmem) Control Register.  Configures FSM in Port                         1 = 8051-Memory directly download enable.                         0 = Normal Register access.
 *     ENABLE_FCPORT_FALCON_CTRL In FC 8G mode, control for Falcon input comes from fcport registers instead of TSC.                         1 = FCport registers control Falcon PMD inputs in 8G FC mode.                         0 = TSC control Falcon PMD inputs in 8G FC mode.
 *     COMCLK_DIV2_CTRL When lcref OR pll_refclk = 212.5Mhz to support 28G PLL freq, the comclk going to PMD needs to be div2.                         1 = div/2 PMD.pmd_refclk_out coming out of PMD and feed it back as PMD.comclk.                         0 = PMD.pmd_refclk_out=PMD.comclk.
 *     MODE_SEL_TX_PI   Mode select for TX_PI, one-hot encoding.                          001 = TX_PI is shut down, CDR Phase from one side to the other is disabled by forcing 0s.                         010 = TX_PI is pass thru, CDR Phase from one side fed to the other.                         100 = TX_PI is port-based. Allows selecting TX_PI from any of the other ports,                                use mode_sel_tx_pi_? to select the port. This mode allows complete muxing 			       of any port's RX_PI to be sent on any port's TX_PI
 *     DISABLE_PI_0     Port 0: Disable PI generation from receiving port to transmit port for mode2:1 and mode1:2. Mode1:1 is enabled by default and cannot be disabled.
 *     DISABLE_PI_1     Port 1: Disable PI generation from receiving port to transmit port for mode2:1 and mode1:2. Mode1:1 is enabled by default and cannot be disabled.
 *     DISABLE_PI_2     Port 2: Disable PI generation from receiving port to transmit port for mode2:1 and mode1:2. Mode1:1 is enabled by default and cannot be disabled.
 *     DISABLE_PI_3     Port 3: Disable PI generation from receiving port to transmit port for mode2:1 and mode1:2. Mode1:1 is enabled by default and cannot be disabled.
 *     FCPORT_CORE_PORT_MODE FCPORT Port Mode.  
 *     REPEATER_MODE    Indicates M2 Quad is in repeater mode(OTP repeater mode bit)
 *     MODE_SEL_TX_PI_0 Mode select for TX_PI Port-0                         00 = Select PI from other side's port-0                         01 = Select PI from other side's port-1                         10 = Select PI from other side's port-2                         11 = Select PI from other side's port-3
 *     MODE_SEL_TX_PI_1 Mode select for TX_PI Port-1                         00 = Select PI from other side's port-0                         01 = Select PI from other side's port-1                         10 = Select PI from other side's port-2                         11 = Select PI from other side's port-3
 *     MODE_SEL_TX_PI_2 Mode select for TX_PI Port-2                         00 = Select PI from other side's port-0                         01 = Select PI from other side's port-1                         10 = Select PI from other side's port-2                         11 = Select PI from other side's port-3
 *     MODE_SEL_TX_PI_3 Mode select for TX_PI Port-3                         00 = Select PI from other side's port-0                         01 = Select PI from other side's port-1                         10 = Select PI from other side's port-2                         11 = Select PI from other side's port-3
 *     MODE_SEL_RX_PI_0 Mode select for RX_PI Port-0                         00 = Send default lane RX-PI to other side                         01 = Force 1to2: Gearbox Mode.                         10 = Force 2to1: Gearbox Mode.                         11 = N/A
 *     MODE_SEL_RX_PI_1 Mode select for RX_PI Port-1                         00 = Send default lane RX-PI to other side                         01 = Force 1to2: Gearbox Mode.                         10 = Force 2to1: Gearbox Mode.                         11 = N/A
 *     MODE_SEL_RX_PI_2 Mode select for RX_PI Port-2                         00 = Send default lane RX-PI to other side                         01 = Force 1to2: Gearbox Mode.                         10 = Force 2to1: Gearbox Mode.                         11 = N/A
 *     MODE_SEL_RX_PI_3 Mode select for RX_PI Port-3                         00 = Send default lane RX-PI to other side                         01 = Force 1to2: Gearbox Mode.                         10 = Force 2to1: Gearbox Mode.                         11 = N/A
 *
 ******************************************************************************/
