/*******************************************************************************
 * CHIP:  PHY8806X
 * REGISTER:  RTS_MHOST_PP_SMBus_Event_Status
 * BLOCKS:   UCSS
 * DESC:     SMBUS Interrupt Status/ Interrupt Clear Register
 * SIZE:     32
 * FIELDS:
 *     SLAVE_RD_EVENT_EN This bit is set when slave hardware detected read transaction directed toward the SMBUS block. Writing a '1' to this position will clear this bit. When this bit is '1', the SMB0_EVENT bit will be '1' in each processor."
 *     SLAVE_TX_UNDERRUN_EN This bit is set when Slave Tx FIFO becomes empty and less then PKT_LENGTH bytes were output on the SMBUS.
 *     SLAVE_START_BUSY This bit is set when slave START_BUSY transitions from 1 to 0. Writing a '1' to this position will clear this bit. When this bit is '1', the SMB0_EVENT bit will be '1' in each processor.
 *     SLAVE_RX_EVENT   This bit is set when the slave receive FIFO holds at least one valid transaction. Writing a '1' to this position will clear this bit. When this bit is '1', the SMB0_EVENT bit will be '1' in each processor.
 *     SLAVE_RX_THRESHOLD_HIT This bit is set when the slave receive FIFO is equal to or larger than the Slave RX_FIFO_THRESHOLD. Writing a '1' to this position will clear this bit. When this bit is '1', the SMB0_EVENT bit will be '1' in each processor.
 *     SLAVE_RX_FIFO_FULL This bit is set when the slave receive FIFO become full. Writing a '1' to this position will clear this bit. When this bit is '1', the SMB0_EVENT bit will be '1' in each processor.
 *     MASTER_TX_UNDERRUN This bit is set when Master Tx FIFO becomes empty and less then PKT_LENGTH bytes were output on the SMBUS.
 *     MASTER_START_BUSY This bit is set when master START_BUSY transitions from 1 to 0. Writing a '1' to this position will clear this bit. When this bit is '1', the SMB0_EVENT bit will be '1' in each processor.
 *     MASTER_RX_EVENT  This bit is set when the master receive FIFO holds at least one valid transaction. Writing a '1' to this position will clear this bit. When this bit is '1', the SMB0_EVENT bit will be '1' in each processor."
 *     MASTER_RX_THRESHOLD_HIT This bit is set when the master receive FIFO is equal to or larger than the Master RX_FIFO_THRESHOLD. Writing a '1' to this position will clear this bit. When this bit is '1', the SMB0_EVENT bit will be '1' in each processor.
 *     MASTER_RX_FIFO_FULL This bit is set when the master receive FIFO become full. Writing a '1' to this position will clear this bit. When this bit is '1', the SMB0_EVENT bit will be '1' in each processor."
 *
 ******************************************************************************/
